t/plugins.t line 214, in subtest 'privileges: a plugin that demands nothing answers null':

  is $c->get('/plugins/privileges', params => { remote => 'x' }), 'null',
    'the transport hands `null` back as the four-character string';

karr #30 is fixed: _request now decodes a body that is a bare JSON scalar, so
that call returns undef and the assertion fails (got: undef, expected: 'null').
It is the only red test in the suite, fixture and live alike.

The claim is the defect, written down as the contract. The second half of the
same subtest -- is_deeply $c->plugins->privileges(...), [] -- still passes, so
API::Docker::API::Plugins is unaffected and needs no change.

The line the fix wants, keeping the subtest's purpose (that the local guard
survives whatever the transport does):

  is $c->get('/plugins/privileges', params => { remote => 'x' }), undef,
    'the transport decodes the bare null to undef (karr #30)';

t/plugins.t was locked to another agent while the transport work ran, so this
was reported rather than changed. t/containers_endpoints.t's equivalent
subtest ('changes: a container with nothing changed is an empty ArrayRef')
asserts only the normalised result and stays green; its comment about the
transport returning the string 'null' is now stale prose, not a failure.

